# Keep LF in everything the MAST compiler and the mastlib packer read.
#
# A .mastlib is a ZIP, and a zip read does NOT get the CRLF normalization a text read does -
# so a file checked out with CRLF on Windows can behave differently inside the packed lib
# than it does in the working tree. Pinning LF here removes the whole class rather than
# relying on remembering it.
*.mast   text eol=lf
*.amd    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.grid   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
# Engine-read media: the engine opens these itself, and CRLF engine-read files have failed
# far away from the cause. The meshes and their material files stay LF too.
*.obj    text eol=lf
*.mtl    text eol=lf
*.png    binary
